KG42.register("source_edge_archive-40b1d55c24f08e7c8726b907",{"id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R006::E::v141-c-R006-E001","paper":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","rule_ref":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R006","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-015"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-464efdadf92efbd8","target":"COMP-f8ab52e76c9b4025","source_occurrence_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R006::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R006::V::settlement.payment","source_unit_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Compensation for flexibility supplied by curtailable and shiftable loads. | Contractual flexibility charges for curtailable disconnectable loads. | Contractual flexibility charges for reducible and disconnectable generators. | Contractual flexibility charges for shiftable profile loads. | Flexibility-provider revenues in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. | Rewards to participants whose resources are activated in response to DSO requirements. | Settlement administration within the SESP market subsystem for local flexibility transactions.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-008","v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g01-ev-015","v141-b-g02-ev03","v141-b-g02-ev12","v141-b-g02-ev24","v141-b-g02-ev32"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"48ab31c6721b48b973c8e0299718fe8cdc3add9316dfc0b9c56bc13d44e076ac","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The SESP, acting as aggregator, receives DSO flexibility requests specifying minimum active-energy variations relative to the forecast baseline, without knowing grid-status information. Scope: DSO upward- and downward-regulation requests in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. The SESP's coordination of corrective actions must give DSO needs maximum priority to avoid over-voltages or transformer over-loads. Scope: SESP coordination of corrective actions in the local flexibility market. Condition: During a DSO-designated yellow-light grid situation. The SESP may send direct control signals overriding local household energy-management decisions. Scope: SESP control authority over local household resource decisions. Condition: During a grid-constrained yellow-light situation. The SESP's forecast must have DSO approval before it is used as the baseline scenario. Scope: Use of SESP forecasts as the flexibility-market baseline. Condition: When a consumption or generation forecast for a flexible asset is to be used as the baseline scenario.","target_definition":"The SESP market subsystem manages local flexibility transactions, including settlement, billing and accounting applications. Scope: Settlement administration within the SESP market subsystem for local flexibility transactions. Flexibility revenues are paid according to the flexibility contracts under the pay-as-contract arrangement. Scope: Flexibility-provider revenues in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. Participants with activated resources are subsequently rewarded according to their flexibility contracts. Scope: Rewards to participants whose resources are activated in response to DSO requirements. Condition: The participant's resources have been activated. The flexibility cost used to determine compensation for curtailable and shiftable loads does not depend on the amount of activated energy. Scope: Compensation for flexibility supplied by curtailable and shiftable loads. Condition: Flexibility from a curtailable or shiftable load is activated. The disconnection cost equals the number of disconnected periods multiplied by the load's disconnection fee. Scope: Contractual flexibility charges for curtailable disconnectable loads. Condition: A curtailable disconnectable load is disconnected. The shifting cost equals the consumption delay multiplied by the cost per time unit established in the load's flexibility contract. Scope: Contractual flexibility charges for shiftable profile loads. Condition: A shiftable load's consumption is delayed relative to its baseline start. Generator-curtailment fees are established in the agreed flexibility contract, with prices specified period by period for reducing or disconnecting generation. Scope: Contractual flexibility charges for reducible and disconnectable generators. Condition: Generation is reduced or disconnected.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The SESP market subsystem manages local flexibility transactions, including settlement, billing and accounting applications. Scope: Settlement administration within the SESP market subsystem for local flexibility transactions.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-015"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-001","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"be In order to run these markets, local traders need the SESP Platform for or sending information, t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A local flexibility market (LFM) is an electricity trading platform to sell and buy flexibility in geographically limited areas like neighbourhoods and small towns. The SESP is the local market platform provider and community aggregator (AGR). At the same time, the SESP is a BRP from the regulatory point of view because it bids in wholesale markets. In order to run these markets, local traders need the SESP Platform for sending information, trading for flexibility, and scheduling actions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-015","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"The domains aﬀected cover from prosumers and DER installations D up to the distribution grid. The zo","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The zones identified as Market and Enterprise comprise three subsystems that make SESP operation possible. They are the market, control and metering systems. The market is responsible for the management of transactions needed to implement the local flexibility market. It covers energy scheduling, flexibility, settlement, billing and accounting applications. The control subsystem is in charge of the management of the orders determined in the market. The metering subsystem manages the data resulting from smart meters (SM) and local controllers (LC) on the field zone."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Compensation for flexibility supplied by curtailable and shiftable loads. | Contractual flexibility charges for curtailable disconnectable loads. | Contractual flexibility charges for reducible and disconnectable generators. | Contractual flexibility charges for shiftable profile loads. | Flexibility-provider revenues in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. | Rewards to participants whose resources are activated in response to DSO requirements. | Settlement administration within the SESP market subsystem for local flexibility transactions.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-008","v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g01-ev-015","v141-b-g02-ev03","v141-b-g02-ev12","v141-b-g02-ev24","v141-b-g02-ev32"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R006-E001","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-015"]},"paper_scope_note":"There is direct basis for the DSO request, positive and negative regulation relative to the baseline, and SESP operational responsibility; the requested quantity must not be treated as actual supply quantity, nor cost management as the request reception interface."}});
